course: dictionary
lesson: 7477
title: Portrait: a picture or a description
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A portrait is a picture of a person, usually of their face. It can be a painting, a drawing or a photo. «Frida Kahlo, a Mexican painter, was badly hurt in a bus crash as a teenager and painted with a mirror above her bed.» A picture an artist makes of themselves is called a self-portrait.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Frida is the painter and she is painting herself, so a self-portrait must be a picture of the artist. Ask: what word would fit here? A picture of a person fits. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check.
explain: Portrait has other meanings too. A writer can give a portrait of a person or place in words, like «a portrait of village life». On a computer or printer, portrait means a page or screen that is taller than it is wide.
fact: A portrait is a painting, drawing or photograph of a person, especially their face.
fact: «Portrait» can also mean a detailed description in words or film, as in «a portrait of village life».
fact: Portrait layout means a page or screen that is taller than it is wide; the opposite is landscape.
fact: A «self-portrait» is a picture an artist makes of themselves.
fact: Early «portraits» needed people to keep still for a while, so smiles were hard to hold.
exercise: «Frida Kahlo painted with a mirror above her bed.» What is a self-portrait? | A map of a city | A poem about the sea | *A picture an artist makes of themselves | A ticket for a bus
exercise: Early «portraits» needed people to keep still for a while. Why were smiles hard to hold? | Because the paint dried too fast | *Because people had to keep still for a while | Because painters did not like people to smile | Because smiling was banned in the past
exercise: Dad says, «Turn the phone to portrait.» What does he mean? | Hold it flat, wider than it is tall | *Hold it tall, taller than it is wide | Shake it hard | Turn it upside down
test: Which word means a detailed description of someone in words, as in «a portrait of village life»? | Frame | *Portrait | Easel | Canvas
test: On a computer, what does landscape mean, the opposite of portrait? | A page with no words on it | A page taller than it is wide | A page in colour | *A page wider than it is tall
exam: A writer gives a portrait of a character in a story. What is the writer doing? | Drawing the character with a pencil | Reading the story aloud to the class | *Describing the character in detail, in words | Taking a photo of the character's room
